s8-3-p23 : Block
s8-3-p23 = prose (cons "Its identity between \((X,G)\) and \((Y,H)\) is equivalent to an equivalence \(e:X\simeq Y\) together with adjacency preservation \(\prod_{x,x':X} H(e(x),e(x'))=G(x,x')\). The truncated finiteness witness carries no further identity data. Node-indexed positions \(p:X\to\mathbb R^2\) move to \(p\circ e^{-1}:Y\to\mathbb R^2\); a selected vertex and dependent property proofs must move along the same structured equivalence. In particular, identifying graph shapes does not authorize leaving their node-indexed data untouched." nil)
